   "narrative_hooks": [
    "Black Friday through Cyber Monday delivers 20-35% of annual revenue in five days; January is the return peak and the cash trough.",
    "Inventory is bought 4-6 months ahead on ocean freight from Asian suppliers with 30% deposits, so a demand miss shows up as a cash crunch two quarters later.",
    "Apparel return rates run 23-26%; returns are recognised as a reserve against revenue and an inventory asset at recoverable value (ASC 606 variable consideration).",
    "Paid social CAC rose sharply after iOS 14.5 privacy changes; contribution margin after CAC on first orders is often negative, so repeat rate decides unit economics.",
    "The 3PL charges per pick, per item and per pallet-month; storage fees spike when slow SKUs accumulate.",
    "Amazon marketplace payouts arrive every 14 days net of fees, so channel mix shifts DSO and the gross-to-net reconciliation.",
    "Common failure modes: SKU proliferation with long-tail dead stock, chargeback spikes from fraud rings, timezone-mismatched order timestamps breaking daily sales reports, and discount codes stacked beyond intended limits.",
    "Sales tax nexus across states (post-Wayfair) and tariff classifications on imports are the main regulatory touchpoints.",
    "Shopify/Klaviyo/Gorgias stack: orders, email events and support tickets live in separate systems with different customer identifiers.",
    "The founder-CEO watches ROAS and AOV daily; the CFO watches cash runway, inventory turns and the revolver borrowing base."
