   "narrative_hooks": [
    "Comparable-store sales is the headline metric; new-store openings mask comp declines in total revenue.",
    "Vendor allowances (co-op advertising, markdown money) reduce cost of sales and are a classic area for aggressive recognition.",
    "Shrink runs ~1.6% of sales; it is estimated between physical counts and trued up at year end, so quarterly margins can be flattered.",
    "Holiday (Nov-Dec) drives 30-40% of annual operating income; inventory is built from August and payables peak in October.",
    "Gift cards create breakage income recognised in proportion to redemption; unredeemed balances are escheatable in many states.",
    "Store leases under ASC 842 put large ROU assets and liabilities on the balance sheet; impairment tests run per store.",
    "Common failure modes: markdown timing games at quarter end, inter-store transfers double-counted in inventory, POS clocks on store local time vs. the ecommerce platform in UTC, vendor chargebacks disputed for months.",
    "Price elasticity differs by category: grocery staples ~-1 to -2, discretionary apparel ~-1.5 to -3; promotions drive stockpiling rather than consumption.",
    "Regulatory touchpoints: sales tax, PCI-DSS for card data, wage-and-hour compliance for store labour, product safety recalls.",
    "The CEO watches comps and traffic; the CFO watches inventory days and lease-adjusted leverage; the chief merchant watches markdown rate and sell-through."
