   "narrative_hooks": [
    "Funds held for merchants sit on both sides of the balance sheet (restricted cash vs. funds payable); misclassifying them as operating cash is a classic restatement.",
    "Settlement with card networks is T+2 while merchant payouts can be T+1 or instant, so the company pre-funds payouts and carries settlement risk.",
    "Chargebacks arrive 30-120 days after the transaction; the dispute reserve is an estimate that lags fraud waves by a quarter.",
    "Loan loss allowances (CECL) are forward-looking; a change in assumptions moves earnings without any cash event.",
    "Webhooks from the processor are delivered at-least-once; duplicate 'payment.succeeded' events double-credit ledgers unless idempotency keys are enforced.",
    "The outbox table bridges the OLTP ledger and the event bus; when the relay lags, downstream analytics under-report volume for hours.",
    "Regulatory touchpoints: money-transmitter licences by state, PCI-DSS Level 1, BSA/AML and KYC obligations, Reg Z for consumer credit, card-network monitoring programs (VAMP 1.5%).",
    "Take rate compression is the structural threat: large merchants negotiate interchange-plus, so growth in volume outpaces growth in net revenue.",
    "Common failure modes: unreconciled settlement differences written off monthly, read-replica lag showing stale balances to customers, double-booked refunds, FX rounding across multi-currency ledgers.",
    "The CFO watches take rate, net revenue retention and loss rate; the VP Eng watches replica lag, outbox depth and webhook retry rate; the Chief Risk Officer watches dispute ratio against network thresholds."
   ]
